@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title DefaultAlgorithmDetector.detect(&cpg, function) — per-function pipeline
start
:ControlFlowAnalyzer — detect loops
(nesting depth, counted-ness) and
recursion (direct / tail, base cases);<<#D3F9D8>>
note right
  Phase 1 (detection/control_flow.rs)
  detect_loops   -> Vec<LoopPattern>   { header, kind, depth, is_counted }
  detect_recursion -> RecursionPattern { kind, base_cases, recursive_calls }
end note
:ComplexityAnalyzer — map loop-nesting +
recursion shape to ComplexityClass;<<#FFF3BF>>
note right
  Phase 2 (detection/complexity.rs)
  estimate_time_complexity -> ComplexityEstimate
  { class, confidence, justification }
  Combine loops vs recursion: keep the worse
  class via ComplexityClass::is_better_than.
end note
:family heuristics — has_midpoint_calculation /
has_visited_tracking / has_memoization_table
-> AlgorithmFamily;<<#C3FAE8>>
note right
  Phase 3 confidence-scored per-family detectors:
  detect_sorting, detect_searching, detect_graph,
  detect_dp, detect_divide_conquer
  (each returns Option<DetectedAlgorithm>).
end note
:DetectedAlgorithm { signature :
AlgorithmSignature { time_complexity } };<<#F1F3F5>>
note right
  Returns Vec<DetectedAlgorithm>
  { family, name, function, key_nodes,
    signature, confidence }
  sorted by confidence (descending),
  filtered by min_confidence (default 0.5).
end note
stop
legend right
  |= colour |= pipeline stage |
  |<#D3F9D8>| Phase 1 — control-flow analysis |
  |<#FFF3BF>| Phase 2 — complexity estimation |
  |<#C3FAE8>| Phase 3 — family heuristics |
  |<#F1F3F5>| result — DetectedAlgorithm |
endlegend
@enduml
